<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jath State</h1><p class="st-meta">1686 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Jath</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Maratha state of the Deccan, ruled by the Daphle family of Chavan Deshmukhs on the dry eastern edge of Satara.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Jath was founded in 1686 when the Chavan family, later known as Daphle, received the deshmukhi of the Jath area from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Adil Shahi</a> sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>. They retained it under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Daphles ruled a dry, drought-prone territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a> and sheep farming. After 1818 the state came under British protection and was grouped among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">Jagirs</a>, later under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>. Few further details of its rulers are widely recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Jath merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bombay-presidency">Bombay Province</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> in 1960. It now lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sangli-state">Sangli</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jath-state.jpg" alt="Jath State" width="320" height="174"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jath_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1686 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jath</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi, Kannada</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jath</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=jath-state" aria-label="Jath State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6727 1544 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jath State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7047 1800L6991 1757M7047 1800L7364 1601M7047 1800L7364 1602M7047 1800L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7047 1800h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7047 1800h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1817&amp;focus=jath-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
